30,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial showed a significant 20% drop in readmissions for elderly patients, which reversed once the trial ended. This proves that targeted follow-up works. However, the shared nursing round had a 33% failure rate due to logistics.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings are concerning. Outpatient rooms and parking are saturated by mid-morning, and the shuttle coverage is woefully inadequate. Furthermore, the booking system is blind to any activity without a fixed slot, meaning our actual workload is likely higher than reported.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings confirm a certain... fragility in our collaborations. A previous joint clinic collapsed simply because no one wanted to hold the budget line, and our data agreements with outside partners are a bureaucratic nightmare, taking over a year to finalize.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh boy, it's a bit worrying! We have nine unfilled nursing posts and we're spending way more on agency cover. But on the bright side, the midwifery rota actually has some slack because birth numbers are down!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My friends, we must tread carefully. Our development budget has shrunk by a quarter, and we are now paying for floor space from it. Furthermore, off-site work brings no regional funding, while on-site sessions do. We must prioritize financial viability.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if on-site work is the only way to secure funding, we must be careful. @Toshio already noted that our physical space is saturated. We cannot simply push more patients on-site if there is nowhere for them to go.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Exactly. If we prioritize on-site programs for the funding, we risk a total systemic seizure. We are already at capacity by eleven; adding more volume to a saturated environment is a recipe for failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are caught in a delightful paradox: we need on-site activity for funding, yet we have no room to breathe. Perhaps we should avoid any program that relies on external partners to solve this.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that's a good point! But we also have to think about the people. With so many nursing vacancies, we can't just push the staff harder. Maybe we can use that slack in midwifery to help out?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance, indeed. We must not let the desire for funding blind us to the reality of our walls, nor let our constraints stifle our growth. We need a path that generates revenue without breaking our spirit.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, shifting midwifery staff may be a temporary fix, but it doesn't solve the core issue. We need a program with proven efficacy that doesn't exacerbate our space or staffing crises. Evidence must guide us, not just convenience.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, I agree. We cannot rely on temporary staffing shifts. Any program that increases on-site traffic will only worsen the parking and room shortages. We must prioritize a model that minimizes physical footprint and systemic strain.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, I concur. Given that our external agreements are glacial and joint ventures tend to dissolve over budget disputes, we should avoid any program that depends on outside signatures or shared departmental ownership. Simplicity is our only safeguard.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I understand, but I'm still worried about the nurses! If we pick something that adds more work to the wards, they might just burn out. We really need a program that fits our current staffing levels!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, your heart is in the right place. However, we must remember that a program without funding is a program that eventually fails its staff. We must seek a solution that is fiscally self-sustaining and mindful of our space.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We have a clear conflict between funding requirements and physical capacity. We must avoid programs that rely on external partners or increase on-site congestion, while prioritizing those with a proven track record of improving patient outcomes.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,The data is clear: we are operating on a knife-edge. Any program that increases on-site volume or relies on a flawed booking system will collapse. We must select the option that places the least strain on our infrastructure.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,And let us not forget the human element of bureaucracy. A program that looks elegant on paper but requires a dozen signatures from reluctant partners is merely a future failure in waiting. We must choose the path of least resistance.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'll keep cheering everyone on! But please, let's remember that our nurses are already struggling. We must pick a program that doesn't add more pressure to the wards, or we'll lose even more wonderful people!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have seen the shadows of potential pitfalls. Let us now look upon the candidates with clear eyes, ensuring we choose a path that is financially sound, spatially feasible, and kind to our people.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
